## jitasm, Hooking.h / Hooking.cpp, Pool.h, StdInc.h

`jitasm.h`, `Hooking.h`, `Hooking.cpp`, `Pool.h`, `StdInc.h`

These are carried verbatim from the original project's source tree, because
they are part of it: `jitasm.h` is Takashi Tosaka's runtime assembler,
`Hooking.h` / `Hooking.cpp` are CitizenFX's `hook2` framework built on it, and
`Pool.h` / `StdInc.h` are the pool accessor and the shared include the original
loader compiled against. The rebuilt hook bodies do not use them; they are kept
so the tree matches the original and so a reader can compare the two hooking
approaches. Their licenses are the upstream ones (jitasm: free use, see its
header; CitizenFX: MIT).

## ZolikaPatch.ini reader

`INI.h`

The loader needs the shipped mod's own parsing rules (duplicate keys are
last-value-wins, an absent key yields the option arm's default, a value must
parse to exactly 1), so `INI.h` is this project's implementation. It keeps the
`INI<>` call shape of the Feather INI parser (Turbine) that the original
source used; no Feather code is included.

## ZolikaPatch and XLivelessAddon

This is an independent, readable reimplementation of ZolikaPatch 7.65 by
Zolika1351. No ZolikaPatch source code from the older source mirror is copied
here; the mirror (which states no license) was used only as a style reference.
The vendored libraries above are separate third-party components, licensed as
described. The SkipLauncher feature descends from XLivelessAddon
(GTAmodding/XLivelessAddon), which also states no license; its behaviour was
reimplemented from the observed feature contract, not copied.

The hook bodies are hand-written transcriptions of the shipped mod's machine
code. They are part of this repository's MIT-licensed code; the original mod's
authorship and the game's rights holders are acknowledged in CREDITS.md.

The repository history carries `GTAmodding/XLivelessAddon` as a merged
ancestor, so the lineage of the SkipLauncher work stays visible in `git log`.
That merge adds history only: its tree is this project's, and no XLivelessAddon
source is copied into it.

## Game data

`catalogue_data.cpp` contains the multiplayer model-name list used for
diagnostic messages. `ooc_payload.h` is the original compressed
`finale2.sco` resource used by OutOfCommissionFix, kept as static data because
the shipped mod carried it as a module resource. `data/finale2.sco` is the
decoded table for research, and `tools/compress_ooc.py` can produce an
equivalent blob. Both are data extracted from the game / the original mod and
remain the property of their respective rights holders. They are included so a
clean checkout builds the complete mod; `tools/extract_data.py` can regenerate
them from files you own.
